  "historical_output_text": " Planting Seeds in a Container Garden\n\n1. Choose a container that's at least 6 inches deep and has drainage holes. The container should be large enough for the plants you want to grow but small enough to be manageable. \n\n2. Fill the container with a good quality, well-draining potting mix, leaving about an inch of space at the top. Use a high quality potting soil as it contains the right balance of nutrients and structure for growing plants in containers. \n\n3. Make small holes or indentations in the soil, about 1-2 inches deep, using your fingers or a pencil. These holes are where the seeds will be placed. \n\n4. Gently place 2-3 seeds in each hole, spacing them evenly. Be careful not to press them in too hard, just cover them lightly with soil.",
